    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe refactor itself is well done \u2014 the `while`-loop generalization and the extracted `isWeekend` helper are clean, idiomatic, and the change is genuinely additive. One structural nit:\n\n- **`PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` field placement.** The new `private static final Set<LocalDate> PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` constant is declared in the middle of the class, wedged between `resolveRegistrationDate()` and `toBusinessDay()`. Standard Java/Spring convention (and the existing convention in this class, where `Owner`'s other fields live near the top) is to group field/constant declarations at the top of the class rather than interleaving them among method bodies. A maintainer scanning `Owner` for its fields would not expect to find one buried between two methods. Move the constant up with the other class fields (or at least the other static declarations) to keep field declarations in one predictable place.\n\nEverything else \u2014 the javadoc updates, the helper extraction, keeping the holiday logic co-located with the existing `toBusinessDay` business-day logic rather than spawning a new utility \u2014 is coherent and reads naturally.",
